  "description": "OMENAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C204 H292 N12 Nd8 Ni6 O80,7(C2 H6 O1),7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4A (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a branched tree with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.481-4.193 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.43-114.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd8Ni6L6(OAc)24(EtOH)6(H2O)2]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
